      "designator": "CS23-0",
      "grouping_at_time": "Subpart D \u2014 Design and Construction",
      "title_at_revision": "Fabrication methods",
      "text": "(a) The methods of fabrication used must produce consistently sound structures. If a fabrication process (such as gluing, spot welding, or heat-treating) requires close control to reach this objective, the process must be performed under an approved process specification.\n(b) Each new aircraft fabrication method must be substantiated by a test programme.",
